<style>
  .container {
    width: 80%;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
    padding-bottom: 10%;
  }

h1, p, li, ol {
  font-family: sans-serif;
  font-weight: 100;
  font-size: 2vmin;
}

.button-container {
  display: flex;            /* Use flexbox for horizontal alignment */
  justify-content: flex-start; /* Align items to the start */
  gap: 10px;                /* Space between the buttons */
  margin-top: 5%;           /* Add margin to the top of the container */
}

.button-wrapper {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;      /* Align button text vertically */
  justify-content: center;  /* Center button content */
  width: 15em;              /* Consistent width for both buttons */
  padding-top: 3%;
  padding-bottom: 3%;
}

.btn-primary {
  font-family: sans-serif;
  font-weight: 100;
  color: white;
  background-color: #5A80FF;
  text-decoration: none;
  border: none;
  width: 100%;              /* Button takes full width of the wrapper */
  height: 3em;
  display: inline-block;    /* Ensure inline-block display for consistency */
  text-align: center;       /* Center text horizontally */
  cursor: pointer;          /* Add pointer cursor for better UX */
  font-size: 2vmin;
}

.btn-primary:hover, .skip-button:hover {
  background-color: #576AA9;
}


.skip {
  position: relative;
  margin-top: 5%;
}

.skip-button {
  font-family: sans-serif;
  font-weight: 100;
  color: white;
  background-color: #5A80FF;
  text-decoration: none;
  border: none;
  width: 10%;              /* Button takes full width of the wrapper */
  height: 3em;
  text-align: center;       /* Center text horizontally */
  cursor: pointer; 
  padding-top: 1%;
  padding-bottom: 1%;
  padding-left: 2%;
  padding-right: 2%;
}

.label {
  font-size: 2vmin;
}

.input {
  font-size: 2vmin;
}

</style>

<div class = 'container'>

<div class = 'skip'>
  <%= link_to 'Skip Waiver', checkouts_pay_path, class: 'skip-button' %>
</div>

<h1>Rental Agreement and Liability Waiver for Wander Sports LLC (Paddle Board Rental)</h1>
<p>This Rental Agreement and Liability Waiver (hereinafter referred to as the “Agreement”) is
entered into between the undersigned renter (hereinafter referred to as the “Renter”) and Wander
Sports LLC (hereinafter referred to as the “Company”). The Renter acknowledges and agrees to
the terms and conditions set forth below:</p>
<ol>
  <li>Rental Period
    <ol type='a'>
      <li>The rental period shall begin on <%= @reservation.start_date %> at <%= @reservation.start_time_hour%>:<%= sprintf('%02d', @reservation.start_time_minute.to_i) %> <%= @reservation.start_time_period%>
.</li>
      <li>Any extensions to the rental period must be agreed upon in writing by both parties.</li>
    </ol>
  </li>

  <li>Rental Fee
    <ol type='a'>
      <li>The Renter agrees to pay the rental fee in full prior to the commencement of the rental period.</li>
      <li>The Renter agrees to pay a refundable deposit of $100 per paddle board to cover the cost of any damage to the equipment.  In the event that equipment is returned undamaged, the deposit shall be refunded to Renter.</li>
      <li>Additional fees, such as late return fees or damages, may be assessed and charged to the Renter at the Company's discretion.</li>
    </ol>
  </li>

  <li>Condition of Equipment
    <ol type='a'>
      <li>The Renter acknowledges that they have inspected the rented paddle board(s) and all
related equipment and have found them to be in good condition, free from defects or
damage.</li>
      <li>The Renter agrees to return the paddle board(s) and equipment in the same condition
as they were received, normal wear and tear excepted.</li>
    </ol>
  </li>

  <li>Responsibility of Renter
    <ol type='a'>
      <li>The Renter agrees to use the rented paddle board(s) and equipment in a safe and
responsible manner and in accordance with any instructions or guidelines provided by
the Company.</li>
      <li>The Renter shall not use the paddle board(s) and equipment while under the influence
of medications, alcohol, or drugs.</li>
      <li>The Renter shall ensure that each individual utilizing the equipment shall be required
to sign this Agreement. In the event the equipment is being used by a minor, a parent
or legal guardian is required to sign on behalf of the minor.</li>
      <li>The Renter acknowledges that they have the necessary skills and experience to safely
operate the paddle board(s).</li>
      <li>The Renter agrees to comply with all applicable laws and regulations while using the
paddle board(s).</li>
    </ol>
  </li>

  <li>Assumption of Risk. The Renter acknowledges that there are inherent hazards and risks
associated with paddle board activities, including but not limited to:
  <ol type='a'>
    <li>Risk of injury from the activity and equipment, including the potential for permanent
disability and death.</li>
    <li>Rollovers or falling that may cause cuts, broken bones, and other injuries, permanent
disability or death. iii. Exposure to water hydraulics or currents, hidden or obvious
obstructions, and/or debris that can cause drowning or other harm.</li>
    <li>Possible equipment failure and/or malfunction.</li>
    <li>Running into objects, persons, or animals, including barely submerged objects and
other hazards that are not visible.</li>
    <li>Negligence, including operator error.</li>
    <li>Prohibited use of equipment under the influence of any substance/alcohol.</li>
    <li>Hazards related to collision, capsizing, sinking, or other hazards that may result in
exposure to the elements, hypothermia, impact of the body upon the water and/or
rocks, injection of water into body orifices, marine life forms, and/or drowning.</li>
    <li>Cold water and heat-related injuries and illnesses, including but not limited to
hypothermia, hyperthermia, heat exhaustion, heat stroke, sunburn, and dehydration.</li>
    <li>Exposure to outdoor elements, including inclement weather, lightning, severe and/or
varied wind, temperature, or weather conditions.</li>
    <li>Attack by or encounter with insects, marine life forms, and/or animals.</li>
    <li>Accidents or illnesses occurring in remote places where there are no available
medical facilities and rescue may be distant and time-consuming.</li>
    <li>Fatigue, chill, and/or dizziness, which may diminish reaction time and increase the
risk of accidents.</li>
    <li>Participation in activities that may include possible exposure to and illness from
COVID-19.</li>
  </ol>
</li>

<p>The Renter acknowledges and affirms that they have been fully informed of and assumes the
inherent hazards and risks associated with paddle board activities as described above. The Renter
understands that the description of these risks is not complete, and that unknown or unanticipated
risks may result in injury, illness, or death.</p>

<li>Release of Liability Waiver of Claims, and Indemnity Agreement
  <ol type='a'>
    <li>In consideration for being permitted to participate in any paddle board activities, the
Renter hereby releases and holds harmless Wander Sports LLC, its members,
employees, representatives, and agents from any and all liability, claims, or causes of
action for personal injury, property damage, or wrongful death arising from the above
activities, whether caused by negligence or otherwise.</li>
    <li>The Renter agrees to indemnify and hold Wander Sports LLC, its members,
employees, representatives, and agents harmless from any injury, disability, death,
loss, or damage to person or property that may occur as a result of engaging in the
above activities.</li>
    <li>The Renter acknowledges that they are not relying on any oral or written
representations or statements made by Wander Sports LLC, other than what is set
forth in this Agreement.</li>
    <li>This release shall be binding to the fullest extent permitted by law. If any provision of
this release is found to be unenforceable, the remaining terms shall be enforceable.</li>
  </ol>
</li>

<li>Declaration of Fitness
  <ol type='a'>
    <li>The Renter declares that they will not participate in this activity if they have any
COVID-19 symptoms.</li>
    <li>The Renter declares that they are physically fit and have no physical or mental
conditions that should preclude them from participating in the chosen activity.</li>
    <li>The Renter declares that they are not participating against medical advice or treatment
and have not been diagnosed by a registered doctor as having a terminal illness.</li>
    <li>The Renter further declares that in the event they feel ill, have any physical
complaints, or sustain an injury during the course of watercraft activities, they will
immediately notify and disembark from the vessel.</li>
  </ol>
</li>
</ol>
<p>By signing below, the Renter acknowledges that they have read and understood this Agreement
and voluntarily agree to be bound by its terms and conditions.</p>


<%= form_with model: @waiver, url: waivers_path, local: true do |form| %>
  
  <div>
    <%= form.label :first_name, "Renter's First Name", class: 'label' %>
    <%= form.text_field :first_name, required: true, class: 'input' %>
  </div>
  <div>
    <%= form.label :last_name, "Renter's Last Name", class: 'label'  %>
    <%= form.text_field :last_name, required: true, class: 'input'  %>
  </div>

  <div>
    <%= form.label :guardian_name, "Guardian name if renter is under the age of 18", class: 'label'  %>
    <%= form.text_field :guardian_name, class: 'input'  %>
  </div>
    
    <%= form.hidden_field :email %>
    <%= form.hidden_field :birth_date %>

  <div>
    <%= form.label :signature, "Typed Signature of Renter or Guardian if Renter is under the age of 18", class: 'label'  %>
    <%= form.text_area :signature, placeholder: "Type your full name as a signature", required: true, class: 'input'  %>
  </div>

  <div>
    <%= form.check_box :authorized, required: true %>
    <%= form.label :authorized, "I authorize the typed name above as my legal signature.", class: 'label'  %>
  </div>

  <%= form.hidden_field :temp_user_id %>

  <div class="button-container">
  <div class="button-wrapper">
    <%= form.submit "Submit Waiver", class: "btn-primary" %>
  </div>
  <% end %>
</div>

</div>
